 the situation is not getting better and you are not able to concentrate, then you must consider using professional chat discussions or psychological wellness tools and techniques.</p>','straight',2,1,1,NULL,'2021-07-14 15:58:16','2021-07-15 16:51:35',4),(408,0.00,2.00,'Absent',174,173,'<p>Social support and emotional security are vital for our development. We depend on peer groups for emotional, social and psychological support. A peer group is, basically, a group of people having similar interests, age group, background or social status.&nbsp;<br>Sometimes, we try to fit in a group that is not right for us. You seem to understand this and do not engage with people who make you uncomfortable. You seem to know what is right and wrong for you.&nbsp;<br>It looks like you take a stand for yourself and your opinions when there is a need. There can be moments of weakness when you tend to go with the flow and succumb to peer pressure. However, you seem to be clear about your dos and don\'ts. You do not seem to compromise with your value system. You might want to continue maintaining it.&nbsp;</p>','straight',9,1,1,NULL,'2021-07-14 15:58:16','2021-07-14 15:58:16',1),(409,3.00,7.00,'Present',174,173,'<p>Being a part of a social group is a great feeling. It brings a sense of belongingness, emotional security and social support. A group of peers can motivate us to do well. On the other hand, it can also deviate us from our path. It depends on what kind of people we are involved with. Lately, you might have been spending a lot of time with your friends. You might have also been neglecting some important things like your studies, family, etc. It seems like you might be doing things out of your comfort zone just because your friends are doing it. It is indicating that you might not be taking a stand for yourself and your opinions.&nbsp;<br>However, it is crucial to know that you might not want to lose your identity. Instead, you can be with people who appreciate who you are.&nbs